    "mapping_notes": [
      "Complete publisher-edition poem (PTS/BJTS), not a line-complete translation of every VRI stanza. Retain both authentic editions and all explicit differences; no missing words, numbers or line alignment are inferred.",
      "Explicit reviewed mapping: publisher chapter-3 poem 58 corresponds to canonical tha-ap60 by complete title, story and colophon evidence. Shared poem numbers or a numeric offset do not establish other mappings.",
      "Complete poem in the publisher PTS/BJTS-based edition, not a line-complete translation of bundled VRI. Preserve source wording, variants, colophons, printed numbering and note ownership; do not infer individual line alignment.",
      "The publisher prints the stock closing in full; VRI retains a peyyala abbreviation at the final numbered stanza. This is original publisher wording, not application-generated expansion.",
      "Eight original notes belong to the poem. The legend colophon omits Thera in the publisher; no word may be supplied.",
      "Nine physical publisher stanza entries contrast with ten numbered VRI stanzas. Publisher local2/global1315 and local4/global1317-1318a-b each contain six lines; local5/global1318c-f has four. Preserve all compound labels and paragraph boundaries. Original note3 records a six-footed verse and note4 a disagreement in division. Note4 metrical-count wording stays exact beside the actual displayed6/4-line layout; no correction or inferred missing line. Do not label the count difference a missing translated verse without line-level evidence.",
      "VRI57\u201362 divides and orders the Bodhi reverence and Buddha speech differently from publisher local1\u20135/global1314\u20131318c-f. No invented per-stanza correspondence.",
      "Publisher local8/global1321 gives fifty-one thousand and fifty thousand aeons. VRI65 has ekapa\xF1\xF1\u0101sasahasse and pa\xF1\xF1\u0101sasatasahasse; retain the differing literal second compound without silently correcting or numerically harmonizing it."
    ]
